# What must never enter the image.
#
# `COPY . .` is the most dangerous line in this Dockerfile. Everything it must
# not copy is exactly what this project holds: `.env` carries seven secrets,
# and `out/` carries photographs of real people's faces along with their
# sessions and their credit ledgers. An image that bakes either one builds,
# boots and serves identically to a correct one -- until it is pushed to a
# registry, at which point the secrets are published and the seven-day
# retention promise in the consent text is false.
#
# THIS FILE IS NOT A COPY OF `.gitignore` AND MUST NOT BE KEPT IN SYNC WITH IT.
# They answer different questions. `.gitignore` asks "should this be in the
# history of a public repository?"; this asks "should this be in a running
# container?". `docs/` belongs in git and not in a container. `assets/places/`
# belongs in both. The two files agree on the dangerous cases by coincidence of
# subject, not by construction, which is why `test/deploy-image.test.js`
# evaluates the rules below against concrete paths rather than diffing them.
#
# Docker's rule is LAST MATCH WINS, so a `!` line below reverses everything
# above it that it matches. Read the negations at the bottom as the exceptions
# they are.

# --- credentials -----------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key

# --- real people -----------------------------------------------------------
# Faces, sessions, accounts, credit ledgers, OAuth verifiers, and the unsent
# blind-check packet. Gitignored for the same reason; an image is a second way
# to publish a directory and needs its own rule.
out
assets/test-photos

# --- documents that stay on this machine ------------------------------------
# The security reviews are gitignored because this repo is public. A public
# registry publishes just as effectively. The rest of `docs/` is simply not
# something a runtime needs.
docs

# --- weight and local state -------------------------------------------------
.git
.github
node_modules
build
logs
review
assets/stock
test
*.md
!assets/fonts/OFL.txt

# --- development-only files -------------------------------------------------
.claude
.vscode
.idea
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose*.yml
